      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:03:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Performance / Allocation in Animation Path:\n`new Rect()` allocates a new object on every call to `gatherTransparentRegion()`. Because `gatherTransparentRegion` is called recursively across the entire view hierarchy, and with this change it will now execute on every animated frame whenever matrix transformations change, this creates significant garbage collection pressure on the UI thread during 60/120fps animations.\n\nPlease reuse a cached rect from `AttachInfo` (e.g., `attachInfo.mTmpInvalRect` or a dedicated scratch rect in `AttachInfo`) instead of allocating a new `Rect` on every view traversal.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "revId": "367516a95758494a892c38d3597c7b9f8aac501e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
