      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:03:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correctness with Rotated / Non-Axis-Aligned Views:\n`getGlobalVisibleRect(rect)` maps the view\u0027s transformed bounds into an axis-aligned bounding box (`child.getMatrix().mapRect(...)`). For non-orthogonal rotations (e.g., 30° or 45°), this bounding box is strictly larger than the view\u0027s actual geometry.\n\nWhen `region.op(..., Region.Op.DIFFERENCE)` is executed, it carves out the entire axis-aligned bounding box, removing transparent area from regions where the view does not actually render content (the empty corners of the bounding box).\n\nFurthermore, note that `SurfaceView.gatherTransparentRegion()` still uses `getLocationInWindow()` and unrotated width/height to punch the transparent hole. If the `SurfaceView` itself is animated or rotated, the punch-through region will remain un-transformed.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "revId": "367516a95758494a892c38d3597c7b9f8aac501e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
